ce reviewed","value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","Creator screenshot rendered by the real game engine through its desktop test simulator.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/butch-graves-j2me.webp","alt","Butch Graves 3D gameplay showing a ghoul approaching the first-person revolver with the phone-sized health and ammo HUD.","https://github.com/WollyMonjac/ButchGraves3D","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[86],"Claude model / chat","Creator evidence",[91],"evidence","section",{"_57":92,"_25":93,"_94":95},"Read the human and Claude contribution disclosure","https://github.com/WollyMonjac/ButchGraves3D#butch-graves-3d","note","The creator explicitly distinguishes human briefs, direction and real-device playtests from the model’s implementation and asset tools. Exact Claude client is not identified; the cloud sandbox alone does not establish Claude Code.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[100],{"_57":101,"_25":75,"_94":102},"Open the complete J2ME game and assets","Full Java game, level/resource packs, procedural art/audio tools, tests and packaged full/lite builds. Rebuilding needs JDK8, a MIDP2.0/CLDC1.0 API JAR, ProGuard and the toolchain paths documented in DEVELOPER.md. No repository code license is declared; fonts retain SIL OFL terms.","Access type","download","demo","Play or run",[108],{"_57":109,"_25":110,"_94":111},"Download Butch Graves 3D","https://github.com/WollyMonjac/ButchGraves3D/tree/main/dist","Ready-built v2.3.0 JAR/JAD files: full game1.7MB or lite build994KB without voices. Requires a compatible MIDP2.0 phone or J2ME Loader, KEmulator or FreeJ2ME; it does not launch with ordinary java -jar. Keypad2/8 moves,4/6 turns,1/3 strafes,5 fires,0 uses,7/9 switches weapons,# jumps and* opens the map. Binary downloaded and inspected, but not executed.","Game platform","Downloadable build","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[119],{"_57":120,"_25":75,"_94":-7},"Read the creator’s build and testing account","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[125,126,127,128],"Download the full or lite JAR and open it in a compatible J2ME emulator or MIDP 2.0 phone.","Try moving, turning, firing, using doors and switching weapons during the opening episode.","Read the creator’s implementation account and compare src/E.java with the generated resource packs.","Change one level or resource, follow DEVELOPER.md to rebuild, and verify the phone API, memory and audio constraints on the target runtime.","AI workflow / foundation context","WollyMonjac credits Claude Opus 5.5 with code, levels, art and audio tools. The human supplied the brief and direction, played builds and reported problems; the creator also explains simulator, emulator and real-device testing separately.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Custom fixed-point raycaster · Java MIDP 2.0 / CLDC 1.0","engine","lead","3d","ai-assisted",[125,126,127,128],{"_57":120,"_25":75,"_17":156},{"_57":109,"_25":110,"_17":104,"_94":111},{"_57":101,"_25":75,"_154":155,"_94":102},{"_57":92,"_25":93,"_94":95},"resourceIds",[],"scope","complete-project","build-log",{"_158":159},"documents",{"_160":161,"_162":163},"en",[165,169,170,171,168,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,167,204,166,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222],"zh",[164,165,166,167,168],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders"